vivo study in vitro studies have been  done that show  that cars have a number of functional  deficits when  you when stimulated by low antigen  density including a lower il-2  production  so our lab has studied this  thoroughly with the c-22 target antigen  found on  hematologic malignancies  however what's emerging in the field and  what's been seen  is that other hematologic antigens such  as cd20 and cd19  are also cars targeting these antigens  are also affected by antigen density  in addition  antigens found on solid tumors such as  anaplastic lymphoma kinase or alk on  neuroblastoma or egfr v3  cars targeting these antigens have also  been found to be affected by antigen  density  and so this lack of engine sensitivity  is a broad phenomenon of car t cells  across target engines and a major area  for improvement in the car t cell field  so we wanted to go back and look at what  parts of the car could be  modified in order to enhance this  response to low antigen density  tumors so in order to really analyze the  structure of the car uh we have to  observe the receptor which it is uh  designed uh to somewhat emulate which is  the endogenous t cell antigen receptor  or tcr  so in contrast to the tcr which  recognizes peptide antigens presented on  tumor cells in the context of mhc  molecules the car redirects t cell  specificity using an antigen binding  domain that's commonly derived from an  antibody variable region which is at the  top of the car and then  this is connected to intracellular  signaling moieties which commonly  include the co-stimulatory domain such  as cd 28 or 41vb as well as the cd3 data  chain from the tcr complex  so some straightforward modifications  have been made to  the car that can have effects on antigen  sensitivity or carb performance and  these include the co-stimulatory domain  and so swapping this out  has been shown to make a difference  as well as the number of immunoreceptor  tyrosine based activation motifs or  itams in the cd3 zeta chain which are  represented in red  however recently our lab and others have  made the observation that portions of  the car construct previously thought to  be almost inert can have large impacts  on car biology  and one of these is the flexible linker  amino acid linker region between the  heavy and light chain in the antigen  binding domain of the car  and so a group at penn made the  observation  and published recently that their car  didn't perform as well in patients as  the c22 car from the trial at the nci  and found that astonishingly one of the  only differences was  in fact the flexible linker domain that  i just showed you  and so  they  wanted to study why this was the case  and so they found that they made a car  with a short linker and these linkers  flexible amino acid linkers commonly  have been constructed from motifs that  consist of four glycine residues  followed by a serine so a short linker  is just one of these motifs and while  their long linker car  had four of these motifs in between the  heavy and light chain of the antibody  and they found that  when they  compared short and long linker cars one  of the major differences was the uh  the long  linker cars were not are able to  permit heavy and light chain pairing on  an individual car  receptor whereas uh g4s by one short  linker does not permit heavy and light  chain pairing and instead favors pairing  of heavy and light chains from distinct  cars which causes antigen-independent  dimerization  and so in the figure on the left here  they show the fluorescent microscopy  that  the shortening of the linker length  induces car clustering  and antigen independent signaling  as compared to the long linker car which  is more homogeneously distributed  throughout the cell  however they also found that when they  compared these two cars that this  antigen independent clustering induced  signaling as well  and tonic signaling of multiple  tcr signaling  pathways including ps3 kinase map kinase  and p53  so  we hypothesized based on the trial  by don terry's child that another  important factor with this short linker  car was not only the ability to do these  things but that this  would enhance the ability to respond to  lower antigen densities seen in  patients treated with c22 car t cells  and so we hypothesized that this would  require that this target engine in  particular requires enhanced and  insensitivity  so we wanted to test these our  short and long linker car t cells  against our range of  leukemias bearing different engine  densities and we found that  in contrast to the short linker car  which  was in the clinical trial when we made a  long linker uh car  that shortening the the short linker car  improved sensitivity to low density  target engines  and so especially when you look at the  cars targeting cd22 low leukemia  you can see that the short linker car  has significantly higher numbers of  cells making  il2 and interferon gamma in response to  a low antigen density stimulation  however as nic 22 cars utilizing scfcs  derived from the m971 antibody clone  bearing these short and long leakers  have already been evaluated in the  clinic we sought to assess how other  modifications to the antigen binding  domain could affect car t cell function  and whether combining these  modifications could further enhance  cartiso responses to low density  antigens  our hypothesis  is that affinity maturation of the car  antigen binding domain will enhance  responses to 22 low leukemia and this  will increase overall therapeutic  efficacy of cars targeting the c22  antigen  so in order to  in order to develop a car with a high  affinity car  our collaborators affinity matured the  m971 binder and this resulted in an scfv  with approximately one thousand fold  higher affinity for cd22 and you can see  this on the left the standard affinity  on the top the high affinity on the  bottom  the  high affinity binder  has approximately a thousand-fold  difference in the  dissociation constant kd  we also wanted a simple cell-based  readout to ensure that when we developed  these binders into  a car into the receptor and transduced t  cells that we would see a similar change  in affinity so we transduced cars into t  cells with either the high affinity or  the standard affinity binder and  incubated these cells with a range of  concentrations of a 404 conjugated c22  protein fc  and in this assay we can see enhanced  car binding of c22  with the high affinity binder  as indicated by the red trace and as  compared to the blue trace and this is  indicated by increased mfi  at lower concentrations of target  antigen indicating that the higher  affinity binder  shows enhanced carb binding  so we went on to test this in vitro and  in contrast to our hypothesis  we found that affinity maturation does  not enhance carbocytokine production in  response to low density target antigens  and in fact when you  compare the top row here the high  affinity car across antigen densities to  the standard affinity car  we found that in general the high  affinity car had lower number of cells  lower numbers of cells making  either il2 or interferon gamma in  contrast to the standard affinity car  we wanted to go on and test this a  little bit further and so we looked at a  signaling a different signaling  molecules that are known to be important  in t cell function  so  again we found that affinity maturation  does not increase the percentage of cars  that phosphorylate essential t-cell  signaling proteins phosphorylation of  the  extracellular signal-related kinases orc  one and two in particular have been  previously identified through silac  analyses in our lab as highly  correlative with car t-cell in vivo  activity  so when we looked at phospho-erc on the  top we found that across antigen  densities there were  fewer high affinity car t cells  phosphorylating earth  as compared to the standard affinity car  we also looked at several other  signaling moieties known to be important  for t cell function  and  these include nf kappa b plc gamma and  p38 map kinase and again we saw that  there really was no difference in these  signaling moieties between the high  affinity and standard affinity car  so then we took these cars  and wanted to do in vivo testing against  our 22 low leukemia and in contrast to  the in vitro data we found that the  affinity matured car enhanced in vivo  responses to  cd2 to low leukemia  so on the left is  uh  radio or radiance data or bioluminescent  imaging data comparing the standard  affinity and high affinity cars  with  luciferase labeled leukemia and we found  that the high affinity card  significantly  increased  early leukemic clearance compared to the  standard affinity cart  and this also manifested in the  increased survival of mice that were  treated with high affinity cars as  compared to standard affinity cars  as you can see on the right  so what i didn't mention was that this  high affinity scfv was sent to us  containing a g4s by 3 linker sequence  which is as i mentioned a longer linker  that does not permit card dimerization  on the cell surface  so after  understanding the biology of this  response further uh we had pos and  seeing this promising in vivo data with  the  high affinity long linker car we then  hypothesized that combining  modifications to the car antigen binding  domain  in particular this affinity maturation  and  shortening of the linker length would  have synergistic effects on car  sensitivity to low density target  antigens  however what we found was that when we  combine these modifications these two  discrete modifications of the engine  binding domain are independent in  boosting in vitro car responses to cd22  low leukemia  so we tested the high affinity long  linker on the top the high affinity  short linker in the middle and  standard affinity short linker on the  bottom  and while we saw  that  in this donor the high affinity longer  actually recruited more cells into the  activated pool producing il2 or infrared  gamma compared to the standard affinity  short linker the high affinity short  linker car performed  worse than both  other cars in this assay  we also looked again at phospho erc and  again found no significant difference  between the three cars in number of  cells phosphorylating earth against 22  low leukemia  however  we obviously wanted to test this car  again in vivo and  see if it improved leukemia clearance  in xenograft models  and what we found  was that although the  high affinity short linker car perhaps  performed slightly  worse in vivo that the  regardless of linker length the high  affinity cards performed very similarly  to each other in vivo and both high  affinity cars outperformed the standard  affinity car in clearance of cd22 low  leukemia and so this can be seen again  by  bioluminescent imaging data  on the left  in that these two cars  both have very similar leukemic early  leukemia clearance relative to  mice treated either with mock t cells or  standard affinity car t cells  and we also looked at survival of these  myosins found that both high affinity  cars significantly increased survival  relative to the standard affinity car  and that both the high affinity cars  were very similar  in their increase of survival  so in conclusion  affinity maturation of the engine  binding domain does not significantly  enhance in vitro car responses to cd22  low leukemia  however when we  tested the affinity matured car  in vivo we found that the affinity  matured high affinity car  outperformed the standard affinity car  in clearance of c22 low leukemia  when we combined the  modifications to the antigen binding  domain  including shortening the linker and  increasing affinity of the binding  domain we found that these discrete  modifications that individually enhance  car function are not always synergistic  in their  increase  in  car functions against 